# docs/play-console/whatsnew.txt

When a user-visible change needs Play Console copy, add it to `docs/play-console/whatsnew.txt` under **the date it was written** (`Date: YYYY-MM-DD`, today unless the user names another day).

- **Append.** Never delete or replace other `Date:` blocks. A version bump or new headline is not a reason to empty the file.
- **Same day.** If that date already exists, add another `Date:` block for the same day. Only replace that day’s `<en-US>` / `<hu-HU>` when the user supplies a full replacement for that date.
- **Both languages.** Always write `<en-US>` and `<hu-HU>`. Each language body (inside the tags only) is **max 500 characters**.
- **Release name.** Keep `next (after X)` until a Play version bump; then change the name. Dated blocks stay.

```
Date: 2026-09-20

<en-US>
Headline.

• Bullet
</en-US>

<hu-HU>
Címsor.

• Pont
</hu-HU>
```
